      "questionType": "response",
      "activityRole": "practice",
      "difficultyBand": 2,
      "dok": 2,
      "calculatorPolicy": "inherit",
      "assessedConstruct": "A.6A",
      "taskType": "representationTranslation",
      "representation": "graph",
      "type": "functionInvestigation",
      "prompt": "Graph $f(x)={{a}}(x-{{h}})^2{{k|signed}}$ by plotting its vertex, then write the domain and range.",
      "functionSpec": {
        "type": "quadratic",
        "a": "{{a}}",
        "h": "{{h}}",
        "k": "{{k}}"
      },
      "pointTasks": [
        {
          "id": "vertex",
          "label": "Plot the vertex",
          "x": "{{h}}",
          "expected": [
            "{{h}}",
            "{{k}}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "analysisRequests": [
        {
          "id": "domain",
          "label": "Domain",
          "kind": "domain",
          "notation": "interval",
          "responseMode": "text",
          "expected": [
            "(-inf,inf)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "range",
          "label": "Range",
          "kind": "range",
          "notation": "interval",
          "responseMode": "text",
          "expected": [
            "[{{k}},inf)"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "An upward-opening quadratic extends forever left and right but has a lowest output.",
        "reasoning": [
          "There is no restriction on x, so the domain is all real numbers.",
          "The vertex $({{h}},{{k}})$ is the minimum, so the range is $[{{k}},\\infty)$."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Separate horizontal extent (domain) from vertical extent (range)."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "The vertex gives the range endpoint; the parabola continues indefinitely in both x-directions."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "a": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 4
          },
          "h": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -4,
            "max": 4
          },
          "k": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -8,
            "max": 8
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mm_A_6A_v2_projectile-context-domain-range",
      "active": true,
      "alignmentKeys": [
        "texas:A.6A"
      ],
      "courseId": "algebra1",
      "familyId": "mathmaster:A.6A:v2-projectile-context-domain-range",
      "familyVersion": 3,
      "questionType": "response",
      "activityRole": "practice",
      "difficultyBand": 3,
      "dok": 2,
      "calculatorPolicy": "inherit",
      "assessedConstruct": "A.6A",
      "taskType": "application",
      "representation": "context",
      "prompt": "A projectile is modeled by $h(t)=-{{a}}(t-{{v}})^2+{{maxh}}$ only from launch until it returns to the ground. Write the reasonable domain of time and the corresponding range of height in interval notation.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "domain",
          "label": "Reasonable time domain",
          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "[0,{{end}}]"
        },
        {
          "id": "range",
          "label": "Height range",
          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "[0,{{maxh}}]"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Context can restrict a quadratic that is mathematically defined for every real input.",
        "reasoning": [
          "Because {{maxh}}={{a}}({{v}})^2, the model reaches ground level at t=0 and t={{end}}.",
          "During the physical flight, time runs from 0 to {{end}} and height runs from 0 to the vertex height {{maxh}}."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Use the physical interval of flight, not the unrestricted algebraic domain of the formula."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "The vertex occurs halfway between the two ground times."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "a": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 3
          },
          "v": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 2,
            "max": 6
          }
        },
        "derived": {
          "maxh": "a*v*v",
          "end": "2*v"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mm_A_6A_v2_restricted-domain-range",
      "active": true,
      "alignmentKeys": [
        "texas:A.6A"
      ],
      "courseId": "algebra1",
      "familyId": "mathmaster:A.6A:v2-restricted-domain-range",
      "familyVersion": 3,
      "questionType": "response",
      "activityRole": "practice",
      "difficultyBand": 3,
      "dok": 2,
      "calculatorPolicy": "inherit",
      "assessedConstruct": "A.6A",
      "taskType": "application",
      "representation": "symbolic",
      "prompt": "For $q(x)={{a}}(x-{{h}})^2{{k|signed}}$ restricted to ${{h}}\\le x\\le {{hi}}$, write BOTH the domain and range in interval notation.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "domain",
          "label": "Domain",
          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "[{{h}},{{hi}}]"
        },
        {
          "id": "range",
          "label": "Range",
          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "[{{k}},{{top}}]"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "A restricted domain changes the range because only part of the parabola is allowed.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The domain starts at the vertex x={{h}} and ends at {{hi}}.",
          "On this right-hand branch the function increases from {{k}} to {{top}}, so the range is $[{{k}},{{top}}]$."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Evaluate the function at the restricted endpoint as well as at the vertex."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Because the domain begins at the vertex and moves right, the outputs increase."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "a": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 3
          },
          "h": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -4,
            "max": 2
          },
          "k": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -6,
            "max": 6
          },
          "span": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 2,
            "max": 4
          }
        },
        "derived": {
          "hi": "h+span",
          "top": "a*span*span+k"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mm_A_6A_v2_downward-range-error",
      "active": true,
      "alignmentKeys": [
        "texas:A.6A"
      ],
      "courseId": "algebra1",
      "familyId": "mathmaster:A.6A:v2-downward-range-error",
      "familyVersion": 3,
      "questionType": "response",
      "activityRole": "practice",
      "difficultyBand": 3,
      "dok": 2,
      "calculatorPolicy": "inherit",
      "assessedConstruct": "A.6A",
      "taskType": "errorAnalysis",
      "representation": "verbal",
      "prompt": "For $g(x)=-{{a}}(x-{{h}})^2{{k|signed}}$, a student writes the range as $[{{k}},\\infty)$ because the vertex y-value is {{k}}. Correct the range in interval notation.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Correct range",
          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "(-inf,{{k}}]"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "The vertex is a maximum when the parabola opens downward.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The negative leading coefficient makes every other output less than or equal to {{k}}.",
          "Therefore the range extends downward without bound and includes {{k}}: $(-\\infty,{{k}}]$."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "First decide whether the vertex is a minimum or maximum."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Opening downward means the vertex is the greatest y-value."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "a": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": 1,
            "max": 5
          },
          "h": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -5,
            "max": 5
          },
          "k": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -9,
            "max": 9
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mm_A_6A_v2_translate-inequality-to-range",
      "active": true,
      "alignmentKeys": [
        "texas:A.6A"
      ],
      "courseId": "algebra1",
      "familyId": "mathmaster:A.6A:v2-translate-inequality-to-range",
      "familyVersion": 3,
      "questionType": "response",
      "activityRole": "practice",
      "difficultyBand": 4,
      "dok": 3,
      "calculatorPolicy": "inherit",
      "assessedConstruct": "A.6A",
      "taskType": "transfer",
      "representation": "multipleRepresentation",
      "prompt": "A quadratic has domain all real numbers, opens {{direction}}, and has vertex $({{h}},{{k}})$. Write its range in interval notation and give the inequality statement that describes the same y-values.",
      "responseFields": [
        {
          "id": "interval",
          "label": "Range in interval notation",
          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "{{interval}}"
        },
        {
          "id": "inequality",
          "label": "Equivalent range inequality",
          "inputProfile": "inequality",
          "expected": "{{ineq}}"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "The same range can be represented as an interval or as an inequality.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The opening direction determines whether {{k}} is the minimum or maximum output.",
          "The endpoint is included because the vertex lies on the graph, so both representations include equality."
        ]
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Make the interval direction and inequality direction agree with the opening of the parabola."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Upward: y is at least k. Downward: y is at most k."
      ],
      "generator": {
        "parameters": {
          "up": {
            "type": "choice",
            "values": [
              0,
              1
            ]
          },
          "h": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -5,
            "max": 5
          },
          "k": {
            "type": "int",
            "min": -8,
            "max": 8
          }
        },
        "derived": {
          "direction": "up==1?'upward':'downward'",
          "interval": "up==1?'['+k+',inf)':'(-inf,'+k+']'",
          "ineq": "up==1?'y>='+k:'y<='+k"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
